#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059481 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2129aee3-923d-57de-8bdc-983ffdf787f1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] :question/id #uuid "2b6e8845-a53d-510c-b44f-1b00271ee507" :question/math-academy-id "e-4434" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A)$, if $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 6 - 2 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&= 18 - 10 \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059482 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26e8a6ff-e5ed-59a7-b31d-1981495bf26a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Non-Integer Entries"}] :question/id #uuid "b066b73a-c777-550c-9c6e-af8093bf7fab" :question/math-academy-id "e-4435" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A)$, if $\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= \\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} - (-2) \\cdot 0 \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059483 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccdde46-a4ab-517e-910b-571a3a166b6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Expression Involving the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "043a5e58-e1a0-50a5-b1be-d404e6262991" :question/math-academy-id "e-4436" :question/problem "If\n${A} = \\left\\lbrack \\matrix {2 & -1 \\ -3 & k} \\right\\rbrack$\nand\n$\\det({A}) = 5$, what is the value of $k$?" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot k - (-1) \\cdot (-3) \\\\\n&= 2k - 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=5$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= 5 \\\\\n2k - 3 &= 5 \\\\\n2k &= 8 \\\\\nk &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
